<div id="2026-11-18-commit-review-fails-closed" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-18 — Commit review always happens or the commit is blocked</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> The commit reviewer now tries primary Sonnet 5.5 at 8000 tokens, the same model again at 12000 after a cut-off or error, the alternate <code>gpt-6-sol</code>, then a free coding model from <code>data/ai_model_chains.json</code> (not vision-only, not under 7B, never grok/glm/Relace). Vendor independence holds at every step. When the $0.50/day cap is hit it goes straight to the free reviewer. The result names the model and step that gave the review. With no parsed review the commit is blocked: <code>Not reviewed, commit blocked: &lt;reason&gt;</code> with a <strong>Retry review</strong> button in the AI Editor commit form; reviewer disabled also blocks. Only an empty diff passes unreviewed.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> A commit went in with <code>Not reviewed: review call failed: OpenRouter reply cut off ... finish_reason=length. Commit is allowed.</code> <code>max_tokens</code> was 1500 and Sonnet 5.5 spent it all thinking, so the gate failed open.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/AI/ReviewGate.pm</code> (new, model order), <code>lib/Comserv/Util/AI/ReviewRun.pm</code> (new, review loop, <code>should_block</code>, <code>gate_view</code>), <code>lib/Comserv/Util/AI/CodeReviewer.pm</code> (delegates), <code>data/ai_reviewer.json</code> (<code>max_tokens</code> 8000, <code>free_models</code>), <code>root/ai2/editor/right_dock_commit.tt</code> (Retry review), <code>t/ai_review_gate.t</code> (new), <code>t/ai_paid_block_and_gates.t</code>. <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Git.pm</code> (dashboard gate, review and confirm; hand edit, approved). Todo #2761.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Dashboard too.</strong> The <code>/admin/git</code> dashboard Commit button now fails closed the same way: no parsed review blocks the commit (click Commit again to retry the review), an unreviewed result is never reused, and confirm or "commit anyway" is refused while not reviewed. Only an empty or data-entry-only diff passes unreviewed.</p>
</div>
